gpu_frame_stats on Vulkan: IssueDraw is timed in 15 sections with the time stamp counter (steady clock off x86):
setup, primitive processing, shader translation, samplers, textures, render target cache update, pipeline, viewport,
dynamic state, system constants, bindings, vertex buffers, shared memory use and barriers, render pass entry, and the
draw itself. Every 10 s, next to 0115's thread CPU times, the log gives the draws per frame, IssueDraw's milliseconds
per frame and nanoseconds per draw, the render pass entries per frame, and each section's nanoseconds per draw, so the
GPU command thread's time splits into IssueDraw and the rest (PM4 processing).

